  "problem": "${lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{-20n}=$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall the following special limit: \n\n$$\ne={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the given limit using the algebra of limits, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{-20n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{[{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n}]}^{-20} \\\\  & ={[{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n}]}^{-20} \\\\  & ={e}^{-20} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{20}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
